WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.107
Domain-specific language can change both vocabulary and meaning.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:09.637
Clinical notes contain abbreviations, medication names, procedure terms,

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:13.522
and writing patterns that are uncommon in general web text.

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:18.062
Legal documents use specialized phrases and document structures.

00:00:18.062 --> 00:00:23.907
Financial filings and scientific papers have their own terminology and style.

00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:30.137
A general pretrained model may still work well, especially if it is large and broadly trained,

00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:37.292
but domain-pretrained or domain-adapted models can be worth testing when specialized terminology matters.

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:41.777
Do not assume that a domain label automatically makes a model better.

00:00:41.777 --> 00:00:46.307
Compare candidates on representative examples from your actual task.

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:49.492
Also inspect the training data and license.

00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:56.287
A clinical model trained on one type of note may not transfer perfectly to another institution or task.

00:00:56.287 --> 00:01:00.130
Domain fit is evidence to investigate, not a guarantee.
